.TH MEMEX 1 "August 2026" "memex 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
memex \- personal memex ingest, search, stats, and compress
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memex
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B memex
is the command for crate
.BR majestic .
It ingests account data exports into mmap archives and searches those archives
with PCRE2.
.PP
The crate lives at
.BR ~/majestic .
The data directory is
.BR ~/memex
(file key
.BR memex_dir ,
default
.BR ~/memex ).
Number 0012 is Majestic Memex and is specified. This command is still a proof
of concept. It is not that numbered specification.
.PP
Search uses mmap text, grep-searcher, and grep-pcre2 only. Patterns are PCRE2
(the same engine as
.BR "rg -P" ).
There is no PCRE1 and no rust-regex fallback.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ingest
Ingest Grok dumps, ChatGPT conversations, Facebook DYI zips, X account
archives, Telegram
.BR result.json ,
session JSONL, markdown, Obsidian, reports, or session_docs sqlite.
With no paths,
.B memex ingest
scans
.B $HOME
for known export shapes. Home scan skips system trash by default. Extra skips
belong in
.B skip_directories
in the config file. Crate defaults do not skip
.BR ~/.agents/trash .
.TP
.B search
Search mmap archives under
.BR ~/memex .
See
.BR memex-search (1)
and
.B SEARCH PATTERNS
below.
.TP
.B stats
Print archive counts. Needs
.B --service
and
.BR --account ,
or an explicit archive path.
.TP
.B compress
Write
.B FILE.zst
next to each uncompressed archive (zstd level 3, no dictionary). Never deletes
the input.
.TP
.B decompress
Write
.B FILE
without
.BR .zst .
Never deletes the
.BR .zst .
.TP
.B mcp
JSON-RPC 2.0 MCP on stdin/stdout. Default is JSON, one object per line.
.B --toon
is Token-Oriented Object Notation for language-model tools (one TOON
document then a blank line). Spec:
.IR https://github.com/toon-format/spec
(accessed: 2026-08-27). Media type
.BR text/toon .
Terminal logs are error and info on stderr. Full logs:
.BR "journalctl --user -t memex" .
.TP
.B serve
The same MCP JSON-RPC over HTTP. Default bind is loopback
.BR 127.0.0.1:8741 .
No auth. No TLS. JSON default.
.B --toon ,
.BR "Accept: text/toon" ,
or
.B format=toon
select TOON. Request
.B Content-Type: text/toon
is accepted.
.TP
.B acp
ACP-shaped NDJSON JSON-RPC on stdin/stdout. JSON default.
.B --toon
is TOON for language-model tools.
.TP
.B bench-zstd
Zstd bench of uncompressed archives. Does not delete sources or Downloads.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --memex-dir " DIR"
Memex data directory. Default is
.BR $HOME/memex .
File key
.BR memex_dir .
Overrides the config file. Global.
.PP
.TP
.B --toon
On
.BR mcp ,
.BR acp ,
and
.BR serve :
respond in TOON (
.BR text/toon )
for language-model tools. Default is JSON for humans. Spec:
.IR https://github.com/toon-format/spec
(accessed: 2026-08-27).
.PP
Subcommand flags such as
.BR -i ,
.BR -F ,
.BR -w ,
.BR --bind ,
.BR --toon ,
.BR --service ,
and
.B --account
override the matching file keys when you pass them. Skip lists have no flags.
They live under
.B [scan]
in the config file. There is no
.B --config
flag. Set
.B MEMEX_CONFIG
to choose another TOML path.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Optional settings live at
.I ~/.config/majestic/memex.toml
(that is
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/majestic/memex.toml
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set). That is not
.I ~/.config/memex/
and not
.IR ~/majestic/memex.toml .
A missing file uses crate defaults. You do not have to create the file.
.PP
Layers are crate defaults, then that TOML file (figment), then
.B MEMEX_*
environment variables, then flags you passed. CLI flags override the file.
Figment overlays layers. confy cannot. The
.B directories
crate supplies the XDG config directory.
.PP
Home scan skips system trash by default: XDG Trash
.RI ( $XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash ,
usually
.IR ~/.local/share/Trash ),
directory name
.BR .Trash ,
and names that start with
.BR .Trash- .
That skip does not include all of
.BR /tmp .
Extra directories belong in
.B skip_directories
on that machine. Crate defaults do not skip
.BR ~/.agents/trash .
A committed example with every key is
.I docs/memex.toml.example
in the crate. That example sets
.B skip_directories
to an empty list and comments one extra path that is not machine-specific.
.PP
Keys:
.BR memex_dir ,
.BR scan.home_scan_max_depth
(default 8),
.BR scan.skip_directories ,
.BR scan.skip_system_trash
(default true),
.BR search.ignore_case ,
.BR search.fixed_strings ,
.BR search.word_regexp ,
.BR search.archive ,
.BR ingest.output ,
.BR ingest.inputs ,
.BR scope.service ,
.BR scope.account ,
.BR stats.archive ,
.BR serve.bind
(default
.BR 127.0.0.1:8741 ),
.BR compress.level
(default 3),
.BR zip.max_uncompressed_bytes
(default 8 GiB),
.BR log.filter
(default
.BR info ),
.BR jobs.rayon_threads ,
.BR bench_zstd.dir ,
.BR bench_zstd.jsonl ,
.BR bench_zstd.report ,
.BR bench_zstd.re_ingest .
Path-valued keys expand a leading
.BR ~ .
.SH SEARCH PATTERNS
Patterns are PCRE2.
.B -i
is case insensitive.
.B -w
is whole word.
.B -F
is a phrase or literal.
.B |
is OR. AND any order uses lookaheads.
.PP
.nf
Want                 Pattern
OR                   lizard|catfooding
AND, any order       (?=.*lizard)(?=.*the)
Phrase               'hello world'  or  -F 'hello world'
Case insensitive     -i
Whole word           -w
.fi
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
memex search 'lizard|catfooding'
memex search '(?=.*lizard)(?=.*the)'
memex search -F 'hello world'
memex search -i catfooding
memex search -w food
.fi
.SH LOGGING
The terminal shows error and info by default. It does not show warn, debug, or
trace. Permission denied is an error. Expected skips are debug in the journal,
not on the terminal. Full logs use syslog identifier
.BR memex :
.PP
.nf
journalctl --user SYSLOG_IDENTIFIER=memex
journalctl --user -t memex
.fi
.PP
Override the terminal with
.B MEMEX_LOG
or
.BR RUST_LOG .
If those are unset,
.B [log] filter
in
.I ~/.config/majestic/memex.toml
applies (default
.B info
means error and info, not warn). The journal always keeps the full log. If
journald is missing, the terminal still works and the journal layer is skipped.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MEMEX_CONFIG
Path to a TOML file. Overrides
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/majestic/memex.toml .
A leading
.B ~
expands to
.BR $HOME .
.TP
.B MEMEX_LOG
Terminal tracing filter. Wins over
.B RUST_LOG
and over
.B [log] filter
in the TOML file. Not a figment overlay of the
.B [log]
table.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Terminal tracing filter when
.B MEMEX_LOG
is unset.
.TP
.B HOME
User home. Default data directory is
.BR $HOME/memex .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base for
.IR majestic/memex.toml .
When unset, memex uses
.IR ~/.config/majestic/memex.toml .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base for XDG Trash
.RI ( $XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash )
when
.B skip_system_trash
is true. When unset, that trash is
.IR ~/.local/share/Trash .
.PP
Other
.B MEMEX_*
variables overlay TOML keys. Nested keys use a double underscore after the
.B MEMEX_
prefix (for example
.BR MEMEX_SEARCH__IGNORE_CASE ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/majestic/memex.toml
Optional user settings
.RI ( $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/majestic/memex.toml ).
A missing file uses crate defaults.
.TP
.I docs/memex.toml.example
Committed example with every key. Not machine-specific.
.TP
.I ~/majestic
Crate source. The command is still a proof of concept.
.TP
.I ~/memex/{service}/{account}.majestic
Archive files. Leftover
.B .archive
files are listed when there is no sibling same-stem
.BR .majestic .
Do not mmap
.BR .zst .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR memex-search (1)
.PP
Crate README and AGENTS.md live in
.IR ~/majestic .
Concise American Technical English
(https://github.com/SurmountSystems/specs/blob/main/0005_CATE.md,
accessed: 2026-08-27).
